    description: "Found during WI-kokuv-dakak-sitop-tinul-jodin-gizoh-namir-dakum (branch jgstern-agent/fix/kokuv, 098155b5a0). linkers/ipc.py detects receivers only via ipcMain.on/.handle/.handleOnce and ipcRenderer.on/.once. A main process that registers handlers through its own wrapper, e.g. podman-desktop packages/main/src/plugin/index.ts:280 `ipcHandle(channel, listener)` called as `this.ipcHandle('containerfile:getInfo', ...)` (containerfile-parser.ts:34, index.ts:472, and many more), yields NO receive site for those channels. Effect, measured with link_ipc on ~/whole_bunch_of_repos/podman-desktop/packages after the kokuv fix: 66 contextBridge bridge callers, 58 distinct preload send nodes, and only 1 bridge caller reaches any ipcMain receiver, so the renderer -> preload -> main chain still stops at the preload for 65 of 66 callers. The send side already accepts custom wrappers (ipcInvoke/ipcSend in _FUNC_BODY_IPC_PATTERN, and the kokuv fix lets those wrapper send sites join receivers); the receive side has no such path. Likely shape of a fix: detect a same-repo function/method whose body forwards its first parameter to ipcMain.handle/on (`ipcMain.handle(channel, ...)`) and treat literal-channel calls to that function as receive sites. That is the same wrapper-forwarding mechanism as the send-side ipcInvoke support, mirrored. Corpus impact beyond podman-desktop: not measured."  # 76f3
    fields: {}  # 76f3
